    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d7730fbc-a3bd-545a-98ca-5aaa680c4e8b" activityNameId="83652cf1-a152-546a-9bf6-c9237bf49686" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 88dfe2fa-a896-419f-ae5e-202467414d43
This process models 1 meter of sewer system infrastructure with vitrified clay pipe, DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3), the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) as well as deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for one meter of sewer system with vitrified clay pipe.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Complete sewer system, DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters Vitrified clay pipe, 300 mm, outer diameter 355 mm, wall thickness 27 mm, 56 kg/m, 2000 kg/m³. A1-A5 and C1-C4
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_88dfe2fa-a896-419f-ae5e-202467414d43.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
